Devteam description for C343-172:  "Crash could occur when monster uses potion
or food to cure stoning or confusion."

I got this one while playing NetHack 4 (more precisely, one I'd hacked to link
to win32a -- TL;DR I have a functioning Windows NetHack 4), and the bug turns
out to be inherited from vanilla NetHack.

The problem is in src/muse.c, function mon_consume_unstone.  This function calls
m_useup and then uses the object structure afterwards.  The fix presented here
is to save the relevant fields of the object structure and use the saved copies
instead of the structure.

I have added this fix to my bugfix repository
(https://github.com/chasonr/nethack-3.4.3-bugfix).

Thanks to Alex Smith and Daniel Thaler.  The NitroHack/NetHack 4 save recovery
system, while it still has its problems, made this bug repeatable.

